       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient's weight, kidney function, and liver function don't change that limit. At doses this high, the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI bleeding, and there's little evidence of added benefit.\n\nPlease check these before we go further:\n- **Typo:** Did you mean 40 mg or 200 mg? Typical dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrates up to 200 mg.\n- **Intentional dose:** If a supervising physician or psychiatrist wants a dose above the labeled maximum, please confirm it with your attending or the pharmacist first. I can then enter it with a note documenting who approved it.\n- **Interacting drugs:** Check for other serotonergic drugs, QT-prolonging drugs, anticoagulants, and MAOIs.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, for example \"sertraline 50 mg PO daily\" or \"200 mg PO daily\". If the 400 mg is confirmed, give me the approver's name and I'll enter it."
      }
